From the P?S8 Google group

---------- Forwarded message ---------
From: cjl <Unknown>
Date: Monday, July 30, 2018 at 11:46:00 AM UTC-5
Subject: Announcing the LINC-8 Restoration Project Group
To: P?S/8 <Unknown>


Anyone here is at least posslbly likely interested in this new group.

While discussions of P?S/8 [and OS/8] are a subset there, the main thrust 
of this group is any hardware or software subject relevant to attempting to 
restore 4 (or perhaps more) LINC-8 machines to complete functionality.  
These are the rarest models of the entire PDP-8 family, and few of them 
survive in any form.  [And parts from one may be needed to get another 
working!]

Only aspects of P?S/8 related to specifics on the LINC-8 will be discussed, 
as most P?S/8 subjects will remain here [the purpose of P/S/8 is generally 
to run on all models; each model may have some of its own issues; the 
LINC-8 has the largest requirement of them all!]

Even if you are just curious about this even rarer part of computer 
history, you are invited to join.

Contact me at CLASystems@gmail,com to be added directly,  Or just post a 
follow up here in a reply with your name and e-mail to use, etc.  Or use 
the formal Google Groups method.  [They all work, whatever floats your 
goat.]

We already have some posts there now, and more to come.  Feel free to join 
in.

See ya on LINC-8 Restoration Project

cjl

